    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nThe driver describes a short period of unresponsiveness after a delayed lunch and believes it was a low glucose episode because he uses insulin, but the witness says his hand twitched before he stopped speaking and cannot remember whether he answered immediately after a sweet drink. No glucose was measured until approximately 25 minutes later, when it was 4.8 mmol/L, and the nurse has no contemporaneous clinical record confirming hypoglycaemia, a seizure or another cause.\n\nHe remembers one similar event about two months earlier, while his partner refers to two episodes on consecutive days; the dates, interval between episodes and exact duration remain uncertain. An emergency note lists possible cardiac syncope and requests further investigation, whereas the driver's own description calls the event a faint; neither document records a firm mechanism or an assessment of recurrence risk.\n\nHe also mentions occasional blurred vision when his glucose changes, but an eye card with corrected 6/6 in each eye is more than a year old and no current retinal or visual field report is available. The nurse records diabetes treatment, the disputed loss-of-awareness history and the visual symptoms as separate issues needing clarification, without automatically classifying the event as a diabetic complication.\n"
    ],
